  "lookalike": {
    "about": "Brands whose names fake sites borrow. `keys`: the names (no dots or hyphens); `official`: the brand's own domains (and their subdomains), which are never look-alikes. A host is a look-alike when it is not official and (1) an official domain sits inside it as whole labels followed by more labels (discord.com.example.ru), or (2) its main label (the one before the public suffix; hyphens removed, then read through `confusables`) is a key read the same way, or within one typing mistake of a key of 6 or more letters (one letter added, dropped, changed, or two side by side swapped), or a key of 5 or more letters with words of `lures` before or after it (discordnitro, freerobux, steamtrade). The Studio trust list overrides this rule (and only this one).",
